Full-boot grep for showCustomSnackBar / [ERR] / "error snackbar" across the whole
cold-boot logcat window: ZERO matches (rc=1, no lines). Compare cycle-1 evidence
(bug-ac3-updatetoken-snackbar-unchanged.log), which showed
`showCustomSnackBar` + `[ERR] msg="error snackbar shown"` immediately following
the identical [FAIL] line at the identical call site — that pairing is now GONE.
The [FAIL] line remains (server-side logging preserved, not silenced), only the
user-facing snackbar was removed, matching the NEARS-2383 diff exactly
(auth_controller.dart updateToken() now just `await authServiceInterface.updateToken();`).

App converges to the guest location-prompt screen ("Find Stores and Items Near
You" / "Log in/ Sign up" / "Set Location") with no error banner, no "unhandled
api response" text anywhere on screen. Screenshot:
docs/qa-evidence/NEARS-2298/ac3-cycle2-no-snackbar-guest-converge.png
(A benign "Module is not available" dialog appeared first, tied to this
