sorry_this_module_is_not_available_in_your_location zone check — unrelated to
the token/401 flow, present regardless of NEARS-2298/2383; dismissed via Ok.)

AC3 met: no error snackbar, no unhandled-api-response state on the first screen.

=== AC4 — force-logout convergence, SAME boot, independent code path ===
Same logcat window, same cold boot:
08-22 00:27:55.359 [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/cart/list http_status=401
  -> ApiChecker.checkApi (api_checker.dart:30) <- CartRepository._getCartDataOnline
08-22 00:27:56.831 [NET] POST endpoint=/api/v1/auth/guest/request
08-22 00:27:57.358 [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/auth/guest/request http_status=200
  <- ApiChecker.checkApi's force-logout path (clearSharedData -> guestLogin) firing

Two DISTINCT stack traces confirmed in the raw log: cart/list's 401 unwinds
through ApiChecker.checkApi (api_client.dart:1133 -> api_checker.dart:30), while
cm-firebase-token's 401 unwinds through AuthController.updateToken directly
(api_client.dart:1154, never touching ApiChecker.checkApi at all) — these are
provably separate call paths, confirming the NEARS-2383 snackbar removal on
updateToken() cannot have suppressed or interfered with ApiChecker's force-logout
firing on cart/list's 401. Force-logout still converges cleanly (no crash, no
ANR, no dead-end) to the guest module-home / login-suggestion state.

AC4 met: force-logout/cart-wipe convergence unaffected by the NEARS-2383 fix.

